Hi everyone.

This patch is a work done in preparation of the next generation noeGNUd.
Currently NetHack and SlashEM do not the visual enhancements I would like
to make to this interface. In the first version of noeGNUd all
enhancements were done within noeGNUd itself. The next generation I would
like other interfaces to benifit from these ideas aswell so I decided to
keep the visual enhancements seperate. Many more enhancements are planned,
some aimed specifically at 3d interfaces, some imporvements to 2d & text.

what does this patch include:

Auto Dungeon Chars:
This patch is aimed a patch writers and allows for easier adding of
dungeon glyphs/tiles by patch creators. It removes the hard-coded
S_foo from rm.h and replaces it with an include of "dgn_char.h".
dgn_char.h is generated by "makedefs -c" using dgn_char.in as input.
simply add you un-numbered glyph into dgn_char.in and makedefs will
recreate / renumber the glyphs input into rm.h.

Dark Room :
this patch splits the dual functionality of the "unexplored/dark area"
glyph into two separate glyphs. one for unexplored areas, and one for dark
parts of a room. a new tile for "Darkroom" areas is also supplied. it only
comes into affect if "lit_corridor" and "color" are both on, it then draws
a black(in tty dark-blue) "." for dark parts of a room. 
one immediate benefit of this, is for example if returning to the gnomish
mines after previous explorations the areas you have already traversed are
now clearly marked out. also, it's easy to distinguish between dark areas
vs unexplored areas.

Passages :
This is new to the visenhance patch.  Visible passageways have now been
added around the corridors.  For now I simply copy/pasted the gnomish
mines' tiles for the stone corridor tiles, they can however have their own
look and "feel".  The "x11-gnome" screenshot demonstrates this.

